---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { downloadUrl } from "../lib/commerce";

const buyHref = "/pricing";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="What Ship Studio is for — intent"
  description="Multi-surface final-mile shipping (sign → release → deploy) vs CI-only green checks and checklist theater. Local portal — vendors stay authority."
  path="/intent"
>
  <section class="section intent-page">
    <p class="intent-kicker">Intent</p>
    <h1>Multi-surface final-mile — not CI theater.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Ship Studio is a <strong>local portal and guide</strong> for the last mile of a cut:
      <strong>sign → release → deploy</strong> (and adjacent human gates). It sequences work
      across CLI, TUI, and Desktop. It does not replace Cloudflare, Polar, Apple, or your CI.
    </p>

    <h2>Who it’s for</h2>
    <ul class="list-clean">
      <li>Indie / multi-repo operators shipping <strong>Web + desktop + optional stores/commerce</strong></li>
      <li>People who can own vendor accounts but should not drown in encyclopedias</li>
      <li>Agent-assisted teams that keep <strong>keys under human control</strong></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What it is not</h2>
    <div class="intent-contrast" role="list">
      <div class="intent-contrast-row" role="listitem">
        <p class="intent-contrast-label">CI-only “ship on green”</p>
        <p class="intent-contrast-body">
          Green pipelines prove build health. They do not Open vendor doors, Put secrets on the
          host, or Confirm listing/submit honesty. Studio sits <em>after</em> CI — the final mile.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="intent-contrast-row" role="listitem">
        <p class="intent-contrast-label">Endless checklist apps</p>
        <p class="intent-contrast-body">
          Another static todo list is not Adaptive Publish. Studio builds a plan from your repo,
          Continues automatable gates, and stops at human gates you must attest.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="intent-contrast-row" role="listitem">
        <p class="intent-contrast-label">Belonging / “shipping community” theater</p>
        <p class="intent-contrast-body">
          No identity product. Value is practical release utility: order, Open, Confirm — not a
          feed or badge wall.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>How honesty works</h2>
    <ul class="list-clean">
      <li><strong>Open</strong> the official portal or <strong>Login CLI</strong> when auth is required</li>
      <li><strong>Confirm</strong> after you finish — Studio does not finish OAuth or store review for you</li>
      <li><strong>Never writes deploy secrets</strong> · never auto-publishes to npm/crates/stores</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="note">
      See also the
      <a href="/docs/scope">scope of service</a>
      and
      <a href="/honesty">why human gates are the product</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="intent-cta">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/demo">Watch demo</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/docs">Docs</a>
      <a class="btn" href={buyHref}>Pricing</a>
      <a class="btn" href={downloadUrl()}>Download</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
